{"title":"Cevian","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Special_Cevians\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Special Cevians</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Finding_Lengths\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Finding Lengths</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cevian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <b>cevian</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line_segment\" title=\"Line segment\">line segment</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ray\" title=\"Ray\">ray</a> that extends from one <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\">vertex</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">polygon</a> (usually a triangle) to the opposite side (or the extension of that side).  In the below diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is a cevian.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd24eea624f880d12f92f3d0633bf8831c7c057.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(100,0)--(10,50)--(0,0)); draw((10,50)--(70,0)); dot((10,50)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(10,50),N); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0,0),SW); dot((100,0)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(100,0),SE); dot((70,0)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(70,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"148\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Special_Cevians\">Special Cevians</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cevian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Special Cevians\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_median\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Triangle median\">median</a> is a cevian that divides the opposite side into two congruent lengths.</li>\n<li>An <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">altitude</a> is a cevian that is perpendicular to the opposite side.</li>\n<li>An <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_bisector\" title=\"Angle bisector\">angle bisector</a> is a cevian that divides the angle the cevian came from in half.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Finding_Lengths\">Finding Lengths</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cevian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Finding Lengths\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd24eea624f880d12f92f3d0633bf8831c7c057.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(100,0)--(10,50)--(0,0)); draw((10,50)--(70,0)); dot((10,50)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(10,50),N); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0,0),SW); dot((100,0)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(100,0),SE); dot((70,0)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(70,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"148\" />\n</p><p>In the diagram, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/6098101e466dc45973d65578c6b44f32d841bbe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{ \\angle ADB} = -\\cos{ \\angle ADC}$\" width=\"209\" height=\"13\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/517d1e9f506ff80c0043306f52486630b5aa7d9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB + \\angle ADC = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" />.  Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2550e4a7beba62dacb7b22ef2ffee013df42f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AD^2 + DB^2 - AB^2}{2 \\cdot AD \\cdot DB} = -\\frac{AD^2 + DC^2 - AC^2}{2 \\cdot AD \\cdot DC}\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cevian&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ceva%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Ceva&#39;s Theorem\">Ceva's Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stewart%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Stewart&#39;s Theorem\">Stewart's Theorem</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Cevian&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018080118\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor vi